An ancient, gnarled tree with five massive roots extending deep into rich earth, each root glowing with a different subtle luminescence, rendered in Vincent van Gogh's signature swirling brushstroke style with bold impasto texture. The tree stands alone on a windswept hill under a turbulent starry night sky with characteristic spiraling clouds in deep blues, vibrant yellows, and earthy ochres. The roots interweave through layers of soil revealing hidden depths, some roots reaching toward underground streams while others grip firmly around weathered stones. The bark shows signs of surviving many storms yet the canopy above flourishes with new growth. Dramatic contrast between the chaotic sky and the grounded stability of the root system below the surface.
